WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.305 --> 00:00:16.170
It wasn't Henry's imagination.

2
00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:20.311
The two teenage girls were definitely acting suspicious.

3
00:00:21.172 --> 00:00:26.134
They grabbed their shopping basket and rushed away, disappearing around the end of the aisle.

4
00:00:26.154 --> 00:00:27.975
"Hey, wait!"

5
00:00:28.335 --> 00:00:29.495
Henry called after them.

6
00:00:29.515 --> 00:00:31.096
"Come back here!

7
00:00:32.072 --> 00:00:33.153
We want to talk to you."

8
00:00:34.153 --> 00:00:37.935
He rushed after the girls, with Maggie and Cole right behind him.

9
00:00:37.955 --> 00:00:40.035
"They did it!"

10
00:00:40.416 --> 00:00:41.416
Maggie exclaimed.

11
00:00:42.236 --> 00:00:43.597
"They stole my money!

12
00:00:44.457 --> 00:00:45.778
I should have known it was them!"

13
00:00:45.798 --> 00:00:50.100
"Just hold on," Henry told her over his shoulder.

14
00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:56.402
"Don't start accusing them of stealing your money until I get a chance to ask them some questions."

15
00:00:57.423 --> 00:01:00.224
They caught up to Jill and Ashley near the back of the store.

16
00:01:01.568 --> 00:01:05.150
The two girls seemed annoyed when they saw the younger kids coming again.

17
00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:08.272
"Why are you following us around?"

18
00:01:08.652 --> 00:01:09.513
Ashley demanded.

19
00:01:09.533 --> 00:01:13.295
"We just wanted to say hi," said Henry.

20
00:01:13.315 --> 00:01:16.937
"Maggie likes to keep in touch with her best customers.

21
00:01:17.837 --> 00:01:18.438
Right, Maggie?"

22
00:01:18.458 --> 00:01:22.640
"Right," Maggie said, glaring at the older girls.

23
00:01:24.001 --> 00:01:27.303
Henry was afraid she was going to say something rude to them.

24
00:01:28.063 --> 00:01:29.084
But she kept quiet.

25
00:01:30.048 --> 00:01:33.710
"So you guys are doing a lot of shopping today, huh?"

26
00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:37.031
Henry said, glancing into the girls' shopping basket.

27
00:01:37.051 --> 00:01:38.792
"Not really."

28
00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:40.913
Jill shot a look at Ashley.

29
00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:43.214
"We were just kidding around."

30
00:01:43.234 --> 00:01:46.755
"That's right," Ashley agreed quickly.

31
00:01:46.775 --> 00:01:49.837
"We're not really buying all this stuff.

32
00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:51.818
See? We're putting it back."

33
00:01:52.698 --> 00:01:56.960
She reached into the basket, grabbed lip gloss, and stuck it back on the shelf.

34
00:01:57.952 --> 00:01:59.973
Jill did the same thing with a pack of gum.

35
00:01:59.993 --> 00:02:02.354
"That's weird," Cole said.

36
00:02:02.374 --> 00:02:06.055
"Why would you pick up all that stuff if you weren't planning to buy it?"

37
00:02:07.356 --> 00:02:08.156
Ashley shrugged.

38
00:02:08.176 --> 00:02:09.697
"I told you.

39
00:02:10.457 --> 00:02:12.778
We were just goofing around, having fun."

40
00:02:12.798 --> 00:02:16.560
"That doesn't seem like much fun to me," Cole commented.

41
00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:21.001
"Well, playing basketball doesn't seem like fun to me," Ashley snapped.

42
00:02:21.021 --> 00:02:23.422
"And boys do that all the time, right?"

43
00:02:24.403 --> 00:02:25.563
Cole was surprised.

44
00:02:26.464 --> 00:02:27.004
"What do you mean?

45
00:02:27.932 --> 00:02:29.173
Basketball is a blast!"

46
00:02:30.453 --> 00:02:31.954
Henry glanced over at Maggie.

47
00:02:32.914 --> 00:02:35.395
She was getting that impatient look on her face again.

48
00:02:35.415 --> 00:02:39.217
"You two aren't fooling me," she burst out.

49
00:02:39.237 --> 00:02:41.578
"I know what you were doing.

50
00:02:42.258 --> 00:02:44.399
You were getting ready to spend my money!"

51
00:02:44.419 --> 00:02:46.720
"What are you talking about?"

52
00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:47.720
Jill asked.

53
00:02:49.121 --> 00:02:50.821
"You know what I'm talking about!"

54
00:02:51.041 --> 00:02:51.882
Maggie went on.

55
00:02:51.902 --> 00:02:55.383
"Someone stole the money from my lemonade stand!"

56
00:02:56.424 --> 00:02:57.264
Ashley laughed.

57
00:02:58.324 --> 00:02:58.905
"Oh, right.

58
00:02:59.685 --> 00:03:00.626
I forgot about that."

59
00:03:00.646 --> 00:03:03.248
"You mean you never found that money?"

60
00:03:03.628 --> 00:03:04.249
Jill added.

61
00:03:04.269 --> 00:03:07.792
"Did you ask Ryan, that kid who's always skateboarding?

62
00:03:08.813 --> 00:03:10.034
He's a troublemaker.

63
00:03:10.874 --> 00:03:13.877
He crashed into my mom's flowers a couple of weeks ago."

64
00:03:13.897 --> 00:03:16.639
"It wasn't Ryan.

65
00:03:17.359 --> 00:03:18.460
It was you two!"

66
00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:19.922
Maggie insisted.

67
00:03:19.942 --> 00:03:22.484
"No, it wasn't," Ashley said.

68
00:03:22.504 --> 00:03:24.966
"Why would we need a few dollars?

69
00:03:25.686 --> 00:03:27.788
We already have—" "Quiet!"

70
00:03:28.236 --> 00:03:30.717
Jill hissed, elbowing her friend in the ribs.

71
00:03:30.737 --> 00:03:34.998
"Oops." Ashley had a guilty expression on her face.

72
00:03:35.838 --> 00:03:36.638
Then she shrugged.

73
00:03:36.658 --> 00:03:39.619
"But what's the big deal?"

74
00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:40.739
she asked Jill.

75
00:03:40.759 --> 00:03:44.380
"We already agreed we're not going to use it."

76
00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.341
"Use what?"

77
00:03:46.781 --> 00:03:48.782
Henry asked, feeling confused.

78
00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.162
What were the girls talking about?

79
00:03:52.022 --> 00:03:53.863
Jill had a guilty expression too.

80
00:03:54.843 --> 00:03:57.784
She reached into the shopping basket and grabbed a candy bar.

81
00:03:58.812 --> 00:04:00.293
She stuck it on a nearby shelf.

82
00:04:01.194 --> 00:04:03.015
"It's nothing," she said.

83
00:04:03.035 --> 00:04:06.798
"Maybe you'd better tell us," Cole suggested.

84
00:04:06.818 --> 00:04:10.280
"Because you two are acting pretty suspicious."

85
00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:13.042
"It's no big deal," Ashley said.

86
00:04:13.062 --> 00:04:16.244
"Jill's mother gave us a fifty-dollar bill.

87
00:04:17.225 --> 00:04:21.288
We were supposed to use it to buy sunscreen and some other stuff we need for summer camp."

88
00:04:22.409 --> 00:04:23.069
Jill nodded.

89
00:04:23.089 --> 00:04:26.732
"We thought my mom wouldn't notice if we bought a few extra things.

90
00:04:27.628 --> 00:04:29.190
But I guess we got carried away."

91
00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:34.996
"Yeah. We realized it when you guys started asking us all those annoying questions."

92
00:04:35.957 --> 00:04:36.717
Ashley shrugged.

93
00:04:36.737 --> 00:04:39.300
"So thanks, I guess."

94
00:04:40.001 --> 00:04:40.841
Henry smiled.

95
00:04:40.861 --> 00:04:43.344
"You're welcome," he said.

96
00:04:44.625 --> 00:04:45.967
Maggie was staring at them.

97
00:04:45.987 --> 00:04:48.930
"You mean you really didn't take my money?"

98
00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.112
"Nope," Jill said.

99
00:04:51.936 --> 00:04:56.417
"Besides we could buy a lot more with my mom's fifty dollars than we could with your two

100
00:04:56.497 --> 00:04:57.598
or three dollars."

101
00:04:57.618 --> 00:05:01.499
"It was much more than that," Maggie corrected her.

102
00:05:01.519 --> 00:05:03.779
"That's why I want to get it back!

103
00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:07.561
I need it so I can take horseback-riding lessons."

104
00:05:09.161 --> 00:05:11.742
"Oh. Good luck," Ashley said.

105
00:05:12.362 --> 00:05:14.062
She sounded more sympathetic now.

106
00:05:14.943 --> 00:05:16.123
Jill seemed thoughtful.

107
00:05:16.143 --> 00:05:19.464
"I just remembered something," she said.

108
00:05:20.412 --> 00:05:25.356
"I saw that little girl Nora grabbing something off the table while you were busy talking to her

109
00:05:25.396 --> 00:05:30.881
brother. I thought she was just getting a napkin or something, but she was pretty close to that

110
00:05:30.961 --> 00:05:34.404
cashbox. And she was acting kind of sneaky."

111
00:05:34.444 --> 00:05:37.046
"Really?" Maggie said.

112
00:05:37.947 --> 00:05:39.528
Henry and Cole looked at each other.

113
00:05:39.548 --> 00:05:44.252
"I guess we know who to investigate next," said Henry.
